# Buttons and actions

## Control height is 40px
`Input`, `Select`, `NumberInput`, `PhoneInput`, `Button` (`md`), `FilterButton`, `RefreshButton` are all `h-10`. A field and a button on the same row therefore line up without tweaks:
- Unlabeled field + button → `FieldActionRow` (or `flex items-center gap-2`).
- Labeled fields in a grid → `items-end` (bottoms align because heights match).
- Never shrink/grow one control with `!h-*` / `py-*` overrides to "make it fit". `Button` `sm` (32px) is for tables, toolbars inside cards and compact lists.
- Use `Select` from `components/Select.tsx` instead of a raw `<select>` with ad-hoc classes.

## Deleting an item in a repeated set → `IconButton`
List rows, table rows, form sub-rows (phone numbers, deal line items, pipeline stages, lost reasons):

```tsx
<IconButton tone="danger" icon={<TrashIcon className="h-4 w-4" />} label={t('delete')} onClick={...} />
```
- `size="sm"` (32px) in tables/lists, `size="md"` (40px) when the row also contains form fields.
- View / edit / reorder actions in the same row use `IconButton` with the default `neutral` tone.
- `label` is required (it becomes `aria-label` + `title`).

## Deleting the record itself or a container → `Button variant="danger"`
Delete lead, delete pipeline, bulk delete, revoke key, disconnect: `<Button variant="danger"><TrashIcon className="h-4 w-4" />{label}</Button>`. Never a gray `secondary` button for a destructive action.

## Confirming
- Deleting **persisted** data always confirms via `ConfirmDeleteModal` (or `setConfirmDeleteConfig` + `setIsConfirmDeleteModalOpen` from `AppContext`). The confirm button is `danger`, Cancel is `secondary`.
- Removing an **unsaved** form sub-row (phone row, line item before save) does not confirm.
- No hand-rolled overlay dialogs with raw red buttons.

## Chips / tags
Remove-from-chip uses a real `<button>` with `XIcon` and an `aria-label`, never a clickable `<span>`.

## Don'ts
- No emoji as icons (🗑).
- No raw `<button className="bg-red-600 …">` / `bg-primary …` — use `Button` / `IconButton`.
- No `Button variant="ghost" className="p-1 h-auto !text-red-600"` — `className` is appended, not merged, so those overrides fight the size classes. Use `IconButton`.
